### JetBrains template
# Covers JetBrains IDEs: IntelliJ, RubyMine, PhpStorm, AppCode, PyCharm, CLion, Android Studio and WebStorm
# Reference: https://intellij-support.jetbrains.com/hc/en-us/articles/206544839

# User-specific stuff
.idea/**

# CMake
cmake-build-*/

# File-based project format
*.iws

# IntelliJ
out/

# mpeltonen/sbt-idea plugin
.idea_modules/

# JIRA plugin
atlassian-ide-plugin.xml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Gateway — secrets and generated material
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real environment files. .env.prod holds acquirer credentials, the API key and
# the PAN encryption key: it must never reach a remote.
# .env.prod
# .env.staging
# .env.local
# .env.prod is deliberately tracked as a template in this public repo,
# so the file that actually holds secrets is this one instead.
# .env.prod.local
# .env.sim is deliberately NOT ignored: every value in it is fake and it is what
# makes `make sim` work without setup.
!.env.sim
# !.env.prod.example

# TLS material. Certificates are generated per environment by `make certs`,
# or issued by scripts/certbot_issue.sh. The Let's Encrypt account key and
# the issued private keys live under nginx/letsencrypt.
nginx/letsencrypt/
nginx/certbot-webroot/*
!nginx/certbot-webroot/.gitkeep
#nginx/ssl/
#*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

# Vault unseal keys and root tokens, if an operator ever writes them down here.
vault-keys*.txt
vault-init*.json

# Database dumps: these contain masked PANs, amounts and wallet addresses.
backups/
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Foundry artefacts from the simulation token deployment.
sim/out/
sim/cache/
sim/lib/
sim/src/
sim/foundry.toml

# Testnet wallets generated for dry runs. Each contains a private key.
testnet-wallet.json
testnet-*-wallet.json
.testnet-token

# Generated by scripts/prodtest.sh. Every one of these holds a live credential
# for the rehearsal stack — database and Redis passwords, the Vault root token
# and unseal key, the gateway API key. They are regenerated on each run, so
# there is never a reason to commit one.
.env.prodtest
.prodtest-unseal-key
.prodtest-root-token
.prodtest-token
.prodtest.lock

# Certificates issued for the production rehearsal, private keys included.
acquirer-certs/
.migration-scratch.db
# Base de scripts/run_gateway_local.py : jetable, recréée à chaque lancement.
.local-gateway.db
.alembic-*.db

# Résultats de validation (suites de chaos, charge). Conservés hors /tmp.
.validation/*.log
.prodtest-credentials
.certbot/
.certbot-venv/
